## Project Structure

```
Datafort/
├── main.py                      # Entry point, starts the login window
├── requirements.txt             # Python dependencies
├── Dockerfile                   # App image (Python 3.10-slim + Tk + MySQL client libs)
├── docker-compose.yml           # MySQL + app services
├── Docker_Tool_installation.md  # Kali Linux install notes
├── final_schema.sql             # Current database schema
├── schema.sql                   # OLDER schema (no lockout columns), kept for history
├── mysql-init/init.sql          # Schema auto-loaded by the MySQL container
├── tests.py                     # Manual key-loading check (not a real test suite)
├── config/
│   ├── config.ini               # Local DB settings
│   └── docker_config.ini        # DB settings used inside Docker
├── crypto/
│   ├── ca.py                    # Root CA creation, CSR signing
│   ├── key_management.py        # User/system key generation, storage, CSR creation
│   ├── crypto_operations.py     # AES-GCM backup encryption, RSA signing/verification
│   └── bruteforce.py            # Login attempt counting and lockout
├── database/
│   ├── db_connection.py         # MySQL connection from config.ini
│   └── db_queries.py            # All SQL: users, requests, backups, audit, messages
├── gui/
│   ├── login_window.py          # Login + registration entry
│   ├── register_window.py       # Registration form (key + CSR generation)
│   ├── main_window.py           # Employee / manager / auditor interface
│   ├── admin_panel.py           # Admin interface
│   ├── backup_tab.py            # (empty placeholder)
│   ├── restore_tab.py           # (empty placeholder)
│   └── signing_tab.py           # (empty placeholder)
├── scripts/
│   ├── init_ca_and_admin.py     # One-time: create CA and first admin
│   └── generate_system_keys.py  # One-time: create system key pair
└── utils/
    └── helpers.py               # (empty placeholder)
```

